      "item_id": "fs-id1165042979713",
      "kind": "example",
      "title": "Example 4.15",
      "position": 3,
      "nearest_heading": "Proof",
      "prompt_text": "Verifying that the Mean Value Theorem Applies For $f (x) = \\sqrt{x}$ over the interval $\\left[\\right. 0 , 9 \\left]\\right. ,$ show that $f$ satisfies the hypothesis of the Mean Value Theorem, and therefore there exists at least one value $c \\in (0 , 9)$ such that $f^{'} (c)$ is equal to the slope of the line connecting $\\left(\\right. 0 , f (0) \\left.\\right)$ and $\\left(\\right. 9 , f (9) \\left.\\right) .$ Find these values $c$ guaranteed by the Mean Value Theorem.",
      "prompt_latex_bits": [
        "f (x) = \\sqrt{x}",
        "\\left[\\right. 0 , 9 \\left]\\right. ,",
        "f",
        "c \\in (0 , 9)",
        "f^{'} (c)",
        "\\left(\\right. 0 , f (0) \\left.\\right)",
        "\\left(\\right. 9 , f (9) \\left.\\right) .",
        "c"
      ],
      "has_solution": true,
      "source_anchor": "fs-id1165042979713",
      "notes": ""
